# The repo versions the code and ships the built site. Anything the public
# harvesters can rebuild in a couple of minutes stays out, so a weekly commit
# doesn't drag megabytes of churn into history forever.

# Regenerable: run scripts\harvest-beplus.ps1 / harvest-max.ps1 / harvest-payback.ps1
data/be-plus.json
data/max.json
data/payback.json

# Identical twin of docs/index.html - that one is the deployed copy
dashboard.html

# Raw crawl archive: 6MB, not read by the build, kept locally as a research record
data/behatsdaa-raw.json

# Logs and scratch
data/refresh.log
*.tmp

# NOT ignored, on purpose - expensive or impossible to regenerate:
#   data/geocache.json          hours of rate-limited geocoding
#   data/behatsdaa-*.json       behind an OTP login
#   data/isracard-online.json   hand-extracted, the site blocks scripted access
#   data/groups.json            the hand-built category and district mapping
